## Common Mistakes & How to Avoid Them

| Mistake | Symptom | Fix |
|---------|---------|-----|
| Capturing state in a closure instead of receiving it as an argument | `error: cannot borrow app as mutable` in handler | Change `let app = ...` to receiving `\|app: &mut App\|` as a handler parameter |
| Rebuilding state inside the view function | View function has side effects; state changes unpredictably | Move side effects out of the view function; state changes only in handlers |
| Not using `.key()` on reordered lists | Hover/focus state "sticks" to the wrong element when list reorders | Add `.key(&item.id)` to each element in a dynamically reordered list |
| Using `.clone()` everywhere | Code is hard to follow; performance suffers | Use references (`&item`) and let the view function own the data |
| Hardcoding colors instead of using `Tone` | App breaks in dark mode; WASM doesn't match native | Always use `Tone::Accent`, `Tone::Surface`, etc.; never hardcode RGB |
| Testing only the happy path | Edge cases break in production | Test: empty state, boundary values (0, max, negative), invalid input |
| Committing without running tests | CI fails; work blocks the team | Always run `cargo test --lib` and `cargo test --test recipes` before commit |

---

## Git Workflow

- Pre-commit hook: Runs `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy`. Bypass only in emergencies with `--no-verify`.
- Commits: Prefix with platform or feature (e.g., "Add X11 input handling", "Improve text rendering").
- Tests: Always run `cargo test --lib` and `cargo test --test recipes` before pushing.

